Z||000002||qwikgta||09-14-2001||09:58 PM||||Welcome, <BR>  Many of the items you want/need you can do yourself real cheep.  Visit a local pick-your-parts lot and walk the lot for a while.  I have found my hood vents, side scoops, spoiler, power rear mirror, bucket seat, 16" GTZ rims and more at our local lot.  walk around and look on other GM cars and even forgein cars too.  As for the short shifter you can do it yourself or have someone you know do it.  I did mine.  Get some spray paint and make sure to prep the parts you are spraying, you can do many things in you engine and it will not look like crap if you prep correct.  I made my own open element air cleaner from the stock 2.5 bottom and a 10" chrome lid.  I used a "10" K&N filter to.  I also just made some clear taillights, I will have pics of them on my webpage soon.   Good luck<P>Rob<BR><P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
